Description of datasets (see column "Dataset").


-- tRNA (transfer RNA, 20 different types)

Data provided by Bernhard Kuhle, based on the publication "Relaxed sequence constraints favor mutational freedom in idiosyn-
cratic metazoan mitochondrial tRNAs" by Kuhle et al. (DOI: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-14725-y). Some labels appeared
in both cytoplasmic and mitochondrial subsets provided by Kuhle, so we have added "Cyto" or "Mito" to all labels in order to
maintain unique labels across the full RNA dataset.


-- rRNA (ribosomal RNA, LSU & SSU)

Data extracted from SILVA, and filtered based on phylogenetic diversity (see Methods in manuscript). Robustness data and
genome annotations available, taxonomic assignment at the species level, but with many genes assigned to uncultured taxa (e.g.
uncultured archaeon), for which e.g. genome size is not trustworthy. Note that for rRNA 'Mitochondria' and 'Chloroplast' are re-
corded as taxonomic identifiers (in the 'Domain' column), representing their vertical inheritance.


-- Scer (Saccharomyces cerevisiae)

Mix of data from NCBI/SGD (coding sequences), RNAcentral (noncoding sequences), supplemented with SGD identifiers. Robustness
data was calculated for cytoplasmic coding RNA and for all noncoding RNA.


-- RFAM (experimental data)

Only Structural complexity and length available. Identifiers refer to RFAM. Secondary structures were obtained from 3D struct-
ures using x3dna. One set of 3D structures contained no pseudo-knots ("No pseudo-knots") and could be directly used to cal-
culate structural complexity. The other set of 3D structures did contain pseudo-knots, which has to be removed prior to cal-
culation of structural complexity ("Removed pseudo-knots").


-- SeqNull (sequence null model)

Randomly sampled secondary structures according to the sequence null model (see paper), 10000 per fixed length. The data does
not explicitly appear in Fig. 3, but has been used to calculate the relative complexity values for all other RNA molecules,
and can be seen in the SI, Fig. S14. For most sets, only complexity values and sequence data were generated. For the datasets
with L=[100,500], only the first 10k molecules from the total sample (100k) were collected. In addition, for these samples,
robustness values were calculated for the first 1k molecules, and motif counts are collected.


-- PheNull (phenotype null model)

Randomly sampled secondary structures according to the phenotype null model (see paper), 10000 per fixed length. These struc-
tures do not have corresponding sequences. Similar to SeqNull, there is motif data for the subsets with L=[100,500].


-- RNAC (RNACentral data, fixed length subsets)

Natural RNA data retrieved from RNACentral of various fixed lengths. Note that here we have robustness values based on full
sampling of all one-step mutants, i.e. slightly more accurate than those based on 100 sampled mutants for the other datasets.

